= Solution
{parent=b}

The <geometric series> converges because the <absolute value> of its common ratio is below one. Its <sum> is
$$
\boxed{\frac4{1-1/3}=6.}
$$

= 5
{parent=Paper 1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=5}

Rearrangement gives the <quadratic inequality> $x^2-3x+1\leq0$. The associated <quadratic equation> has roots $(3\pm\sqrt5)/2$. Since the coefficient of $x^2$ is positive, the <quadratic inequality> holds between these roots, including the endpoints:
$$
\boxed{\frac{3-\sqrt5}{2}\leq x\leq\frac{3+\sqrt5}{2}.}
$$

